      "ar": "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ",
      "en": "Peace be upon you",
      "au": "01_10_01_01.mp3",
      "notes": "Standard Islamic greeting."
    },
    {
      "ar": "وَعَلَيْكُمُ السَّلَامُ",
      "en": "And upon you be peace",
      "au": "01_10_01_02.mp3",
      "notes": "Standard response greeting."
    },
    {
      "ar": "هَذِهِ صُورَةُ أُسْرَتِي",
      "en": "This is a picture of my family",
      "au": "01_10_01_03.mp3",
      "notes": "Demonstrative pronoun هَذِهِ (feminine) used because صُورَة ends in Tā' Marbūṭah. Possessive suffix ـِي attached to أُسْرَة (my family)."
    },
    {
      "ar": "مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ",
      "en": "Masha'Allah",
      "au": "01_10_01_04.mp3",
      "notes": "Expression of praise or awe ('As Allah has willed'). No trailing punctuation."
    },
    {
      "ar": "مَنْ هَذَا ؟",
      "en": "Who is this? (M)",
      "au": "01_10_01_05.mp3",
      "notes": "مَنْ (who) + هَذَا (masculine demonstrative 'this')."
    },
    {
